---
// Goal: say where every question goes by default, how the key stays safe,
// and how to point ThinkThen at another backend.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Terminal from '../../components/Terminal.astro';
import { KEY_VARIABLE } from '../../data/catalog.mjs';
import { run } from '../../data/samples.mjs';

const dryRun = run('install/backends', '1-dry-run');
---
<Base title="Backends" description="Where every question goes by default, how the key stays safe, and how to point ThinkThen at another backend.">
  <h1>Backends</h1>
  <p class="lede">A backend is an address and a model. By default, ThinkThen sends every question to Jev, a System One model from TypeSafe.</p>

  <h2>See the plan first</h2>
  <p><code>--dry-run</code> prints what a command would send, and stops. It reads no key and sends nothing.</p>
  <Terminal run={dryRun} caption="The plan names the address, the model, and the variable a key would come from. It holds no key." />
  <p>The plan holds the evidence. Treat a plan with the same care as the request itself.</p>

  <h2>The default</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Setting</th><th>Default</th><th>Set it with</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Address</td><td><code>https://api.typesafe.ai/v1</code></td><td><code>--url BASE</code>, then <code>THINKTHEN_BASE_URL</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Model</td><td><code>jev-latest</code></td><td><code>--model NAME</code>, or <code>model</code> in a question file</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p><code>jev-latest</code> follows the vendor's newest model. Name a version to hold a run to one model.</p>

  <h2>The key</h2>
  <p>The key comes from <code>{KEY_VARIABLE}</code> and from nowhere else. No flag and no file carries one. A missing key exits 4. The message names the variable and never a value.</p>
  <p>The key goes only to the address you named. It never shows in a plan, a result, a saved answer, a log line, or an error.</p>
  <p>A plain <code>http://</code> address may reach only this machine. Any other <code>http://</code> host is a usage error before a request leaves. The key would otherwise cross the network in clear text. Under <code>http://</code> the tool also ignores every proxy variable.</p>
  <p>An address with a user name, a query, or a fragment is a usage error. The plan prints the address, and a saved answer keeps it.</p>

  <h2>Another backend</h2>
  <p>Any server with the same interface can answer. Name it with <code>--url</code> or <code>THINKTHEN_BASE_URL</code>. <a href="/learn/beatles-bench/backends/">Bring your own backend</a> shows how to check one, and why it needs a new bar.</p>

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/reference/">Saved answers and usage counts</a> · <a href="/trust/">Test it before you trust it</a></p>
</Base>
